\strong{Seasonality.} For \code{llt} and \code{ets}, the seasonal component is
\eqn{s_t = \sum_{k=1}^K a_k \sin(2\pi k t/P) + b_k \cos(2\pi k t/P)}, with
\code{t} the number of weeks since 1970-01-01 (so the phase is common to all
keys) and \code{P = period}. When \code{harmonics = NULL}, \code{K} ranges over
\verb{0..max_harmonics} and is chosen by
\eqn{AICc = -2\ell + 2p + 2p(p+1)/(n-p-1)}, where \eqn{\ell} is the
log-likelihood of the trend model on the seasonally adjusted series and
\code{p} counts the trend parameters plus \verb{2K} seasonal coefficients. The
backfitting starts from an OLS fit of a quadratic time trend plus the
harmonics, then \code{n_backfit} times fits the trend on \code{y - s} and
regresses \code{y - trend} on the harmonics; a final trend fit on the last
adjusted series gives the output.

