\item \code{ets}: \code{fable::ETS(error("A") + trend(c("A", "Ad")) + season("N"))} on
the adjusted series, with \code{NA} weeks linearly interpolated (ETS does not
accept missing values). \code{trend} and \code{trend_filtered} are both the
filtered level; \code{trend_se} is \code{NA}. Requires tsibble, fable and
fabletools.
\item \code{stl}: \code{stats::stl(s.window = "periodic", robust = TRUE)} with frequency
52 on the interpolated series. It has its own periodic seasonal
component (no Fourier terms, \code{K = NA}) and a 52-week period instead of
